DSH-Android patch 23: llm-service-lite (vendored @snnh/dsh-llm-service-lite 0.2.1), encrypted
reasoning replay on the OpenAI Responses wire (#84). Applies on top of 14, 16, 17, 18, 22.

OpenAI's Responses API refuses a follow-up request whose `function_call` item carries its server id
(`fc_…`) without the `reasoning` item (`rs_…`) it was produced with. Upstream only replayed that item
when the profile declared `responsesEncryptedReplay` (nothing does), asked for its payload only when
a reasoning level was chosen, and dropped a reasoning item whose summary was empty, encrypted
payload included. So the first tool call of a session on an OpenAI reasoning model broke the next
request. Now:
 - an `openai-reasoning*` family model on `openai-responses` replays encrypted reasoning unless the
   profile says otherwise, and the request asks for `reasoning.encrypted_content` with or without a
   chosen level;
 - a reasoning item with an empty summary but an encrypted payload is kept as an empty reasoning
   block (the app does not show empty reasoning), so its payload reaches the replay metadata;
 - an assistant turn whose reasoning item is not replayed verbatim (history from before this
   patch, another route or model) is sent without the provider's item ids: text, calls, results and
   `call_id` pairing are unchanged, so old sessions keep working instead of failing every request.

